>Gay, D., T. Saunders, S. Camper, and M. Weigert. <year>1993</year>. Receptor editing: an approach by autoreactive B cells to escape tolerance. <source>J. Exp. Med</source>. <volume>177</volume>:<fpage>999</fpage>&#x02013;1008.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8459227</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal">Tiegs, S.L., D.M. Russell, and D. Nemazee. <year>1993</year>. Receptor editing in self-reactive bone marrow B cells. <source>J. Exp. Med</source>. <volume>177</volume>:<fpage>1009</fpage>&#x02013;1020.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8459201</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal">Radic, M.Z., J. Erikson, S. Litwin, and M. Weigert. <year>1993</year>. B lymphocytes may escape tolerance by revising their antigen receptors. <source>J. Exp. Med</source>. <volume>177</volume>:<fpage>1165</fpage>&#x02013;1173.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8459210</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal">Casellas, R., T. Shih, M. Kleinewietfeld, J. Rakonjac, D. Nemazee, K. Rajewsky, and M.C. Nussenzweig. <year>2001</year>. Contribution of receptor editing to the antibody repertoire. <source>Science.</source> <volume>291</volume>:<fpage>1541</fpage>&#x02013;1544.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11222858</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal">Melamed, D., R.J. Benschop, J.C. Cambier, and D. Nemazee. <year>1998</year>. Developmental regulation of B lymphocyte immune tolerance compartmentalizes clonal selection from receptor selection. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>173</fpage>&#x02013;182.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9458042</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal">Zhuang, Y., P. Soriano, and H. Weintraub. <year>1994</year>. The helix-loop-helix gene E2A is required for B cell formation. <source>Cell</source>. <volume>79</volume>:<fpage>875